  "result": "Perfect! All 193 tests pass. I've successfully added a credit note system for handling refunds.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH and NOT_ISSUED errors** to src/errors.js for credit note validation\n\n2. **Created src/credits.js** with `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)`:\n   - Creates refund credit notes for issued invoices\n   - Works with invoices having status: 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n   - Returns `ok(creditNote)` with:\n     - `number`: CN-prefixed number (e.g., CN-2024-0001)\n     - `invoiceNumber`: reference to the original invoice\n     - `customerId`: customer ID\n     - `amount`, `reason`, `date`: credit note details\n   - Separate counter from invoices (CN numbers independent from INV numbers)\n   - Counter resets each year\n   - Errors:\n     - NOT_ISSUED: if invoice is draft\n     - AMOUNT_INVALID: if amount is not positive integer\n     - DATE_INVALID: if date is invalid\n     - CREDIT_TOO_HIGH: if amount exceeds invoice total\n\n3. **Added 12 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Credit note creation for various invoice statuses\n   - Status-based filtering (issued, partially_paid, paid, excludes draft)\n   - Amount validation and limits\n   - Date validation\n   - Sequential numbering with separate counters\n   - Year-based counter reset\n   - Mixed invoice/credit note number handling\n\nThe credit note system maintains independent numbering from invoices while allowing both types of numbers in the existingNumbers array.",
